   615 				; Step $09 - Menu banner logo: assembly-embed Assets/MENU.RAW (320x36 = 11520
   616 				; bytes, Convertor/make_logo.py --export 15) straight into MENU_BANNER_VRAM -
   617 				; same "select bank, then org+ins" idiom as Load_Palette1/Load_Palette2 above.
   618 				; The 4K MEMAC window can't take it in one go, so it is 3 stages, one per bank
   619 				; ($30/$31/$32 = 4096 + 4096 + 3328 bytes), each naming its chunk on the
   620 				; loading screen.  Their 3+3+2 progress dots replace the old ramp-load and
   621 				; MENU.RAW disk-load stages.  Runs after clear_vbxe, so the
   622 				; boot-time VRAM clear can't wipe it.  The banner's palettes (sets 1-3) have no
   623 				; data at all - Apply_Menu_Palettes (view1024.asm) generates the ramps.
   624 					org LOAD_ADDRESS + $400
