  1072 				; Fill_Pal_Preview_Cmap - stage the P-preview's 2x2 grid into CRAM_Buffer
  1073 				; (TL is left at the buffer's zero default = palette 0) then expand the
  1074 				; whole buffer into real CRAM via the existing Setup_Cmap1.  Called once
  1075 				; from Selector_Handle_P (ui.asm).
  1076 				;
  1077 				; Repurposes BLT_MENU_SEP_CLEAR (bcbs.asm) rather than adding a 13th BCB -
  1078 				; it was the separator's boot-time constant fill, but the separator is now a
  1079 				; 160-byte table loaded straight into VRAM (Load_Menu_Sep, init_vbxe.asm), so
  1080 				; this is its only user.  The 12 BCBs already in bcbs.asm exactly fill the
  1081 				; $100-$1FF VBXE VRAM budget (see the memory-map comment at the top of this
  1082 				; file); a 13th BCB overflowed BLT_NFO_NAME_CLEAR across the $200 boundary
  1083 				; into the NTSC_Palette load and corrupted it - do not add a new BCB here.
  1084 				; Its fixed Dest_Step_X (1) and And mask (0, constant source) already match;
  1085 				; Dest_Step_Y0/1 and Width-1/Height-1 are patched once, up front, since they
  1086 				; don't vary between the 3 kicks (only Dest_Adr/Xor do).
